From 3ab7c9eb5108f1c33bbc46fe24f9e21b16d87e7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirill Mitrofanov <kmitrqq@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:19:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_adsp: add X1E80100 ADSP/CDSP for
 Linux at EL2

Without a hypervisor, the X1E80100 ADSP and CDSP can be started like on SDM845/SC7280:
Linux copies the images into the carveouts and releases the core through the QDSP6SS
boot FSM, without TZ PAS. The X1E specifics:
- a second image (the DSP DTB) in its own carveout, plus the DTB descriptor at
  qdsp6ss+0x60..0x74 that a reset clears;
- EVB is the ELF entry, keeping the other bits of the register;
- the clock/PLL bring-up and the stop sequences recovered from the hypervisor (QHEE),
  replayed as raw MMIO, and the CDSP IOMMU apertures QHEE grants;
- TZ is used once, to stop the ADSP image UEFI leaves running.

New compatibles: qcom,x1e80100-adsp-pil, qcom,x1e80100-cdsp-pil.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
